6295:3.1.2 <office:document>(Single OpenDocument XML Files)
6297:The <office:document> element is the root element of a document in OpenDocument format which is represented as a single XML document. It contains the entire document. 
6299:The <office:document> element is a root element.
6301:The <office:document> element is usable within the following elements: <db:component> 12.25.5 and <draw:object> 10.4.6.2.
6303:The <office:document> element has the following attributes: grddl:transformation 19.320, office:mimetype 19.379 and office:version 19.390.
6305:The <office:document> element has the following child elements: <office:automatic-styles> 3.15.3, <office:body> 3.3, <office:font-face-decls> 3.14, <office:master-styles> 3.15.4, <office:meta> 3.2, <office:scripts> 3.12, <office:settings> 3.10 and <office:styles> 3.15.2.
6315:3.1.3.2 <office:document-content>
6317:The <office:document-content> root element contains document content and automatic styles used in a document. The file within a package for the <office:document-content> element is content.xml. 
6319:The <office:document-content> element is a root element.

